1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:05,950
♪ Make way, make way, for the King of the Mountain!

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,850
♪ Bow down low to the best-dressed cat around!

3
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:13,050
♪ (Hide your tails! Hide your ears!)

4
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,990
♪ (Eolssigu!)

5
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:22,110
♪ Who will go? Who will go?

6
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:26,150
♪ Not me, not me, oh no, no, no!

7
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:30,050
♪ (Up where the tigers are? Oh no!)

8
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,610
♪ Send the shrimp!

9
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:32,410
♪ (Too small!)

10
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:33,570
♪ Send the whale!

11
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:35,010
♪ (Too tall!)

12
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:36,410
♪ Send the eel!

13
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:38,410
♪ (Too slippery!)

14
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:40,700
♪ Send nobody at all!

15
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:41,530
♪ (Eolssigu!)

16
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:46,310
♪ Who will go? Who will go?

17
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:50,350
♪ Not me, not me, oh no, no, no!

18
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,680
♪ (Up where the tigers are? Oh no!)

19
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:54,710
♪ Who… will… go?

20
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:02,402
The bottom of the Southern Sea.

21
00:01:02,792 --> 00:01:08,083
A rabbit, tied with kelp, before the Dragon King.

22
00:01:08,953 --> 00:01:13,650
The cure for my sickness is inside that rabbit.

23
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:17,611
Doctor, you may begin.

24
00:01:18,361 --> 00:01:21,379
Hold still, little one.

25
00:01:21,769 --> 00:01:25,802
The King cannot wait.

26
00:01:26,672 --> 00:01:27,714
Steady.

27
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:30,343
Look at me.

28
00:01:30,913 --> 00:01:35,084
You said we were friends.

29
00:01:36,134 --> 00:01:41,539
The terrapin who brought him here could not say a single word.

30
00:01:42,229 --> 00:01:43,440
A knife.

31
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:44,823
A king.

32
00:01:45,213 --> 00:01:48,502
A rabbit a mile under the sea.

33
00:01:48,892 --> 00:01:51,637
How does he ever get home?

34
00:01:53,497 --> 00:02:00,222
Twelve days earlier, that terrapin crawled onto dry land for the first time.

35
00:02:01,092 --> 00:02:03,014
Well, hello there, stranger.

36
00:02:03,284 --> 00:02:04,210
Nice shell.

37
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:06,851
Are you lost, or just slow?

38
00:02:08,591 --> 00:02:13,991
♪ Hold on to my shell, hold on to my shell,

39
00:02:16,591 --> 00:02:21,991
♪ I won't let you fall, I won't let you fall.

40
00:02:24,591 --> 00:02:27,091
♪ (Hold on, hold on…)

41
00:02:34,881 --> 00:02:36,897
Welcome back to the yard!

42
00:02:37,227 --> 00:02:38,856
Pull up a straw mat.

43
00:02:39,186 --> 00:02:42,765
I sing, I tell, and I play every part.

44
00:02:43,305 --> 00:02:46,319
Tonight's tale is two hundred years old.

45
00:02:46,649 --> 00:02:51,553
A king, a rabbit, and a very slow hero.

46
00:02:52,093 --> 00:02:56,223
And when a singer hits a good one, the whole yard shouts back.

47
00:02:56,493 --> 00:02:57,766
Like this!

48
00:02:58,516 --> 00:02:59,657
That's it!

49
00:02:59,657 --> 00:03:00,342
Go on!

50
00:03:01,092 --> 00:03:02,593
Oh, come on.

51
00:03:02,863 --> 00:03:05,609
A seasick fish is louder than that!

52
00:03:06,359 --> 00:03:07,435
That's it!

53
00:03:07,705 --> 00:03:08,656
Go on!

54
00:03:08,656 --> 00:03:09,923
Sing it!

55
00:03:10,673 --> 00:03:16,798
Stay to the end, and I promise you three answers.

56
00:03:18,598 --> 00:03:23,555
Why a mighty Dragon King needed a tiny rabbit.

57
00:03:25,355 --> 00:03:31,215
How the slowest creature in the sea made a tiger cry for his mother.

58
00:03:32,955 --> 00:03:38,686
And what one little rabbit said, with the whole sea waiting to hear.

59
00:03:42,286 --> 00:03:45,358
Based on an old Korean folktale.

60
00:03:45,628 --> 00:03:48,630
Voices and songs were made with AI.

61
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:06,411
Long ago, under the Southern Sea, stood a palace of coral and blue tile.

62
00:04:06,951 --> 00:04:10,629
And on its throne sat the Dragon King.

63
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:12,154
Mighty.

64
00:04:12,484 --> 00:04:13,325
Wise.

65
00:04:13,325 --> 00:04:17,021
And very, very hungry.

66
00:04:17,831 --> 00:04:20,343
More seaweed soup!

67
00:04:20,613 --> 00:04:22,611
More rice cakes!

68
00:04:22,881 --> 00:04:25,434
More of everything!

69
00:04:26,184 --> 00:04:29,943
Majesty, that was your ninth bowl.

70
00:04:30,813 --> 00:04:33,223
Then this is the tenth.

71
00:04:33,493 --> 00:04:36,083
Count properly, Flounder.

72
00:04:36,833 --> 00:04:40,848
He had built a brand-new hall, so he threw a feast.

73
00:04:41,118 --> 00:04:42,529
For one day.

74
00:04:42,799 --> 00:04:44,090
Then two.

75
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,586
Then forty.

76
00:04:46,336 --> 00:04:51,187
Majesty, perhaps a little walk?

77
00:04:51,517 --> 00:04:55,683
Around the hall, just once?

78
00:04:56,493 --> 00:04:57,265
Walk?

79
00:04:57,265 --> 00:05:01,127
Kings don't walk, Doctor!

80
00:05:01,457 --> 00:05:05,995
Kings are carried!

81
00:05:06,805 --> 00:05:12,875
On the fortieth night, the Dragon King stood up to dance.

82
00:05:13,145 --> 00:05:16,686
And fell flat on his royal face.

83
00:05:18,426 --> 00:05:21,441
Doctor Catfish felt the King's pulse.

84
00:05:21,831 --> 00:05:24,457
His long whiskers trembled.

85
00:05:25,327 --> 00:05:26,262
Hmm.

86
00:05:26,262 --> 00:05:28,132
Hmm-hmm.

87
00:05:28,132 --> 00:05:29,534
Hmmmm.

88
00:05:30,284 --> 00:05:33,529
Say something that isn't hmm!

89
00:05:34,279 --> 00:05:35,819
Majesty.

90
00:05:36,209 --> 00:05:46,782
Your pulse is slow, your belly is huge, and your heart is heavy.

91
00:05:47,652 --> 00:05:49,621
I knew all that!

92
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:51,308
Cure it!

93
00:05:52,058 --> 00:06:01,113
The ancient book says only one thing will cure you.

94
00:06:01,443 --> 00:06:06,854
The liver of a rabbit.

95
00:06:07,664 --> 00:06:09,061
A rabbit?

96
00:06:09,391 --> 00:06:12,204
What in the sea is a rabbit?

97
00:06:13,014 --> 00:06:18,044
A land animal, Majesty.

98
00:06:18,314 --> 00:06:20,098
Long ears.

99
00:06:20,368 --> 00:06:27,619
Lives high on the mountains, far above the waves.

100
00:06:28,369 --> 00:06:29,582
Up there?

101
00:06:29,912 --> 00:06:33,821
Where the air is dry and the tigers are hungry?

102
00:06:34,631 --> 00:06:37,590
I built a hall of pearl.

103
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:43,040
And now I cannot even sit up in it.

104
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:55,370
♪ I built a hall of coral with a roof of ocean blue,

105
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:59,870
♪ I threw a feast for forty days and ate the ocean too,

106
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:04,970
♪ The seaweed soup, the rice cakes piled higher than the tide,

107
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:09,970
♪ And now there's thunder rumbling in my royal inside!

108
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:15,390
♪ Oh, my royal belly! Oh, my royal head!

109
00:07:16,020 --> 00:07:19,570
♪ The mighty Dragon King is stuck in his royal bed!

110
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:22,870
♪ (Long live the King! Long live the King!)

111
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:28,400
♪ If the great old doctors came riding down the sky,

112
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:34,170
♪ They'd feel my pulse and shake their heads and tell me not to cry,

113
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:36,120
♪ (Hmm, hmm, hmm!)

114
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:38,900
♪ Your pulse is slow!

115
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:42,660
♪ Your belly's wide!

116
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:46,310
♪ Your heart is heavy, Majesty!

117
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:53,520
♪ (And your crown is on sideways!)

118
00:07:56,420 --> 00:08:00,530
♪ A king can rule the waters, a king can rule the waves,

119
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:08,180
♪ But who can rule a tummy ache? Not even kings are brave…

120
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:15,690
♪ Oh, my royal belly! Oh, my royal head!

121
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:19,770
♪ The mighty Dragon King is stuck in his royal bed!

122
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:23,770
♪ (Long live the King! Long live the King!)

123
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:27,520
♪ Somebody… fetch me… something!

124
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:31,992
Call the whole court.

125
00:08:32,262 --> 00:08:36,238
Tomorrow, someone goes up to the land.

126
00:08:46,288 --> 00:08:51,084
The next morning, the whole court crowded into the throne hall.

127
00:08:51,894 --> 00:08:54,787
My loyal ministers.

128
00:08:55,177 --> 00:08:59,759
Which of you will go up to the land and bring me a rabbit?

129
00:09:00,629 --> 00:09:02,228
Nobody moved.

130
00:09:02,498 --> 00:09:05,145
Somewhere, a shrimp coughed.

131
00:09:05,895 --> 00:09:08,199
An excellent question, Majesty.

132
00:09:08,469 --> 00:09:11,320
I suggest the General.

133
00:09:12,070 --> 00:09:12,657
Me?

134
00:09:12,657 --> 00:09:15,004
I'd love to!

135
00:09:15,274 --> 00:09:17,828
I'd go today!

136
00:09:18,098 --> 00:09:23,593
But, well, on land, humans catch octopus.

137
00:09:24,073 --> 00:09:27,764
They hang us on a line and dry us.

138
00:09:28,154 --> 00:09:31,428
For snacks.

139
00:09:32,028 --> 00:09:35,088
I suggest the Doctor.

140
00:09:35,838 --> 00:09:40,354
I am needed here, to say hmm.

141
00:09:44,234 --> 00:09:48,484
♪ I'd go myself this very day, I'd swim up to the sand,

142
00:09:48,534 --> 00:09:54,884
♪ But both my eyes are on one side, I'd walk in circles on the land!

143
00:09:54,934 --> 00:09:58,684
♪ Who will go? Who will go?

144
00:09:58,734 --> 00:10:03,084
♪ Not me, not me, oh no, no, no!

145
00:10:03,134 --> 00:10:06,724
♪ (Up where the tigers are? Oh no!)

146
00:10:08,134 --> 00:10:12,484
♪ I've got eight arms for fighting, and I'd fight with every one,

147
00:10:12,534 --> 00:10:18,344
♪ But humans hang us on a line and dry us in the sun!

148
00:10:19,434 --> 00:10:28,804
♪ I'd go, but I'm the doctor, and a doctor has to stay,

149
00:10:29,334 --> 00:10:40,154
♪ Somebody must be here to frown and say "hmm" every day!

150
00:10:43,534 --> 00:10:48,984
♪ We'd go, but we walk sideways, we would never reach the shore,

151
00:10:49,034 --> 00:10:54,984
♪ We'd end up somewhere sideways and be lost forevermore!

152
00:10:55,034 --> 00:10:58,784
♪ Who will go? Who will go?

153
00:10:58,834 --> 00:11:02,824
♪ Not me, not me, oh no, no, no!

154
00:11:03,134 --> 00:11:06,724
♪ (Up where the tigers are? Oh no!)

155
00:11:07,034 --> 00:11:08,284
♪ Send the shrimp!

156
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:09,084
♪ (Too small!)

157
00:11:09,134 --> 00:11:10,244
♪ Send the whale!

158
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:11,684
♪ (Too tall!)

159
00:11:11,734 --> 00:11:13,084
♪ Send the eel!

160
00:11:13,134 --> 00:11:15,084
♪ (Too slippery!)

161
00:11:15,134 --> 00:11:17,374
♪ Send nobody at all!

162
00:11:17,424 --> 00:11:18,204
♪ (Eolssigu!)

163
00:11:19,134 --> 00:11:22,984
♪ Who will go? Who will go?

164
00:11:23,034 --> 00:11:27,024
♪ Not me, not me, oh no, no, no!

165
00:11:27,334 --> 00:11:29,354
♪ (Up where the tigers are? Oh no!)

166
00:11:29,404 --> 00:11:31,384
♪ Who… will… go?

167
00:11:34,274 --> 00:11:40,798
And then, from the very back of the hall, a small, slow voice.

168
00:11:41,668 --> 00:11:43,359
I will go, Majesty.

169
00:11:44,109 --> 00:11:45,848
Who said that?

170
00:11:46,178 --> 00:11:48,602
I can't see anyone.

171
00:11:49,412 --> 00:11:51,328
Down here, Majesty.

172
00:11:51,598 --> 00:11:52,769
I'm on my way.

173
00:11:53,039 --> 00:11:54,687
I'll be there in a moment.

174
00:11:55,437 --> 00:11:56,744
The terrapin?

175
00:11:57,074 --> 00:11:59,963
He's the slowest creature in the sea!

176
00:12:00,773 --> 00:12:03,710
He looks after the royal inkstones.

177
00:12:03,980 --> 00:12:06,266
Has anyone ever even noticed him?

178
00:12:07,016 --> 00:12:07,723
No, sir.

179
00:12:07,993 --> 00:12:10,069
But I can breathe air.

180
00:12:10,339 --> 00:12:15,064
My kind can walk on land and swim in the sea.

181
00:12:15,814 --> 00:12:19,914
Why would you risk your little shell for me?

182
00:12:20,664 --> 00:12:24,405
Because once, Majesty, you saved it.

183
00:12:24,735 --> 00:12:26,768
You don't remember.

184
00:12:28,568 --> 00:12:33,521
Long ago, a baby terrapin got tangled in a fisherman's net.

185
00:12:34,061 --> 00:12:35,783
He kicked and kicked.

186
00:12:36,263 --> 00:12:40,272
Every fish swam past him.

187
00:12:40,752 --> 00:12:42,081
Nobody stopped.

188
00:12:42,771 --> 00:12:46,532
Then a young Dragon Prince swam by.

189
00:12:46,862 --> 00:12:50,215
He tore the net open with one claw.

190
00:12:51,025 --> 00:12:53,591
Go on, little one.

191
00:12:53,591 --> 00:12:54,303
Swim.

192
00:12:56,103 --> 00:12:58,860
Nobody else ever stopped for me.

193
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:02,111
I've been yours ever since, Majesty.

194
00:13:02,921 --> 00:13:06,204
I'd forgotten that prince.

195
00:13:06,684 --> 00:13:10,031
What is your name, terrapin?

196
00:13:10,991 --> 00:13:13,019
Steady, Majesty.

197
00:13:13,289 --> 00:13:17,008
Mother said I was slow, but I always got there.

198
00:13:17,758 --> 00:13:22,089
Then go, Steady, my Lord Terrapin.

199
00:13:22,359 --> 00:13:24,496
Bring me a rabbit.

200
00:13:25,246 --> 00:13:26,632
Yes, Majesty.

201
00:13:26,902 --> 00:13:28,615
Only, Majesty.

202
00:13:28,885 --> 00:13:31,531
What does a rabbit look like?

203
00:13:32,281 --> 00:13:34,205
Silence again.

204
00:13:34,475 --> 00:13:38,630
Nobody in the whole sea had ever seen one.

205
00:13:50,820 --> 00:13:54,545
So they sent for the finest painter under the sea.

206
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:57,583
Master Inkwell, the squid.

207
00:13:58,393 --> 00:13:59,776
A rabbit?

208
00:14:00,046 --> 00:14:06,503
I have painted a thousand fish and one very angry lobster.

209
00:14:06,773 --> 00:14:08,060
Describe it!

210
00:14:08,540 --> 00:14:12,751
And I use my own ink.

211
00:14:13,081 --> 00:14:14,854
Very personal.

212
00:14:15,664 --> 00:14:21,849
Eyes like red jewels.

213
00:14:22,119 --> 00:14:29,281
Ears as long as bamboo leaves.

214
00:14:30,031 --> 00:14:31,164
And fins!

215
00:14:31,434 --> 00:14:33,338
Surely it has fins.

216
00:14:33,608 --> 00:14:35,616
Everything has fins.

217
00:14:36,366 --> 00:14:40,625
No fins, Minister.

218
00:14:40,895 --> 00:14:43,557
A nose that twitches.

219
00:14:43,827 --> 00:14:51,063
A tail like a ball of cotton.

220
00:14:51,813 --> 00:14:54,224
A cotton tail?

221
00:14:54,554 --> 00:14:57,641
Oh, this is going to be my masterpiece!

222
00:15:02,631 --> 00:15:04,581
♪ Bring me my brush! Bring me my stone!

223
00:15:04,631 --> 00:15:07,861
♪ Grind me the blackest ink I own!

224
00:15:08,981 --> 00:15:12,431
♪ Paint the eyes that gazed on the mountains of the world,

225
00:15:12,481 --> 00:15:16,031
♪ Paint the mouth that nibbled orchids, every petal curled,

226
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:19,631
♪ Paint the ears that heard the cuckoo calling in the rain,

227
00:15:19,681 --> 00:15:26,031
♪ Paint the nose that sniffed the mist on the fairy mountain chain!

228
00:15:26,081 --> 00:15:28,831
♪ Draw me a rabbit, draw me a rabbit,

229
00:15:28,881 --> 00:15:32,731
♪ Dip in the ink and draw me a rabbit!

230
00:15:32,781 --> 00:15:35,481
♪ (Swish! Swish! Swish!)

231
00:15:35,781 --> 00:15:37,711
♪ Front feet short!

232
00:15:37,761 --> 00:15:38,931
♪ (Short!)

233
00:15:39,681 --> 00:15:41,401
♪ Back feet long!

234
00:15:41,451 --> 00:15:42,491
♪ (Long!)

235
00:15:43,381 --> 00:15:45,051
♪ Ears stand up!

236
00:15:45,101 --> 00:15:45,851
♪ (Up!)

237
00:15:47,581 --> 00:15:50,461
♪ A tail like a puff of cotton!

238
00:15:50,511 --> 00:15:51,511
♪ (Puff!)

239
00:15:53,081 --> 00:15:56,931
♪ Paint the legs that bounded where the spring flowers grow,

240
00:15:56,981 --> 00:16:01,431
♪ Paint the fur that kept him warm in the winter snow,

241
00:16:01,481 --> 00:16:04,631
♪ Are you sure it has no fins?

242
00:16:04,681 --> 00:16:08,271
♪ Not one! Now hush, I'm painting!

243
00:16:08,581 --> 00:16:11,231
♪ Draw me a rabbit, draw me a rabbit,

244
00:16:11,281 --> 00:16:14,831
♪ Dip in the ink and draw me a rabbit!

245
00:16:14,881 --> 00:16:18,211
♪ (Swish! Swish! Swish!)

246
00:16:21,281 --> 00:16:24,731
♪ The half-moon rabbit on the mountain high

247
00:16:24,781 --> 00:16:28,821
♪ Was never as fine as this one, say I!

248
00:16:31,881 --> 00:16:34,531
♪ Draw me a rabbit, draw me a rabbit,

249
00:16:34,581 --> 00:16:37,131
♪ Dip in the ink and draw me a rabbit!

250
00:16:37,181 --> 00:16:39,241
♪ (Swish! Swish! Swish!)

251
00:16:39,781 --> 00:16:44,591
♪ Here you are, Lord Terrapin, take it and go!

252
00:16:48,611 --> 00:16:50,283
And there it was.

253
00:16:50,613 --> 00:16:54,239
A perfect rabbit, in wet black ink.

254
00:16:55,049 --> 00:16:56,286
One rule.

255
00:16:56,556 --> 00:16:58,569
Do not get it wet.

256
00:16:59,319 --> 00:17:00,932
Master Inkwell.

257
00:17:01,202 --> 00:17:03,382
We live in the sea.

258
00:17:04,132 --> 00:17:06,887
Then don't get it very wet.

259
00:17:07,637 --> 00:17:12,809
Steady rolled up the portrait and tucked it under the edge of his shell.

260
00:17:14,549 --> 00:17:18,028
At the palace gate, the court came to see him off.

261
00:17:18,358 --> 00:17:19,957
Well, some of it.

262
00:17:20,767 --> 00:17:22,218
Seaweed lunch.

263
00:17:22,548 --> 00:17:24,296
Seaweed snack.

264
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:28,096
And a spare seaweed, in case.

265
00:17:28,906 --> 00:17:30,528
Listen, Terrapin.

266
00:17:30,798 --> 00:17:35,213
If you meet a tiger, just be bigger than the tiger.

267
00:17:35,963 --> 00:17:38,523
I'm not bigger than anything, General.

268
00:17:39,273 --> 00:17:41,121
Then bite.

269
00:17:41,511 --> 00:17:45,335
Your kind bites hard.

270
00:17:45,725 --> 00:17:51,416
And once you bite, you never let go.

271
00:17:52,286 --> 00:17:53,248
Bite.

272
00:17:53,248 --> 00:17:55,750
Never let go.

273
00:17:56,020 --> 00:17:57,265
Yes, General.

274
00:17:58,015 --> 00:18:03,663
And the smallest officer in the Southern Sea turned his nose up to the light.

275
00:18:15,523 --> 00:18:17,107
Up he swam.

276
00:18:17,437 --> 00:18:19,774
Past the kelp forests.

277
00:18:20,104 --> 00:18:22,857
Past the sleeping whales.

278
00:18:23,397 --> 00:18:26,568
Higher than he had ever been in his life.

279
00:18:27,378 --> 00:18:30,209
Steady, Steady.

280
00:18:30,599 --> 00:18:33,254
One flipper, then the other.

281
00:18:33,644 --> 00:18:35,618
That's all a journey is.

282
00:18:36,218 --> 00:18:39,349
I've never been higher than the kelp.

283
00:18:39,829 --> 00:18:43,866
What if the dry world doesn't want me?

284
00:18:58,256 --> 00:19:01,606
♪ Down in the blue where the lanterns sway,

285
00:19:01,656 --> 00:19:05,006
♪ I polish the inkstones every day,

286
00:19:05,056 --> 00:19:08,106
♪ Nobody sees me, nobody knows

287
00:19:08,156 --> 00:19:12,526
♪ The slowest shell in the palace rows.

288
00:19:12,856 --> 00:19:16,306
♪ But up past the kelp and up past the foam,

289
00:19:16,356 --> 00:19:19,306
♪ There's a world that's never been my home…

290
00:19:19,356 --> 00:19:21,806
♪ Up where the dry things grow,

291
00:19:21,856 --> 00:19:25,206
♪ Where the pine trees lean and the warm winds blow,

292
00:19:25,256 --> 00:19:29,706
♪ I'll go, I'll go, though I'm small and slow,

293
00:19:29,756 --> 00:19:33,346
♪ Up where the dry things grow!

294
00:19:42,056 --> 00:19:45,406
♪ Mother would say when the tide was high,

295
00:19:45,456 --> 00:19:48,206
♪ "The fish can't see it, but there's a sky,

296
00:19:48,256 --> 00:19:51,006
♪ A sky so wide that it has no floor,

297
00:19:51,056 --> 00:19:54,006
♪ And a sun as warm as an open door."

298
00:19:54,056 --> 00:19:57,506
♪ Steady, steady, one flipper at a time,

299
00:19:57,556 --> 00:20:02,036
♪ Slow as the tide, but I'll get there fine.

300
00:20:05,056 --> 00:20:08,406
♪ The King who saved me long ago

301
00:20:08,456 --> 00:20:11,406
♪ Needs one small terrapin now, and so…

302
00:20:11,456 --> 00:20:14,926
♪ Up where the dry things grow,

303
00:20:16,856 --> 00:20:20,206
♪ Where the pine trees lean and the warm winds blow,

304
00:20:20,256 --> 00:20:24,706
♪ I'll go, I'll go, though I'm small and slow,

305
00:20:24,756 --> 00:20:28,346
♪ Up where the dry things grow!

306
00:20:38,856 --> 00:20:41,906
♪ Steady, steady, one flipper at a time,

307
00:20:41,956 --> 00:20:46,436
♪ Slow as the tide, but I'll get there fine.

308
00:20:48,366 --> 00:20:52,462
And then his nose broke the surface.

309
00:20:52,792 --> 00:20:53,702
Sun.

310
00:20:53,702 --> 00:20:54,839
Wind.

311
00:20:55,169 --> 00:20:57,853
Pine trees on red rocks.

312
00:20:58,663 --> 00:21:00,874
So this is dry.

313
00:21:01,204 --> 00:21:03,016
It's very dry.

314
00:21:03,346 --> 00:21:05,028
It's dry all the way up!

315
00:21:05,568 --> 00:21:06,125
Fish!

316
00:21:06,125 --> 00:21:08,914
Fish swimming in the air!

317
00:21:09,184 --> 00:21:09,626
No.

318
00:21:09,626 --> 00:21:10,511
Birds.

319
00:21:10,781 --> 00:21:13,264
Mother said they're called birds.

320
00:21:14,014 --> 00:21:16,967
A seagull looked at Steady.

321
00:21:17,237 --> 00:21:20,188
Steady bowed to the seagull.

322
00:21:20,458 --> 00:21:22,068
The seagull left.

323
00:21:22,818 --> 00:21:23,781
Thank you.

324
00:21:24,051 --> 00:21:25,622
Lovely to meet you.

325
00:21:25,892 --> 00:21:27,999
I'm from the sea.

326
00:21:28,749 --> 00:21:31,160
So he started up the mountain.

327
00:21:31,490 --> 00:21:33,819
One flipper, then the other.

328
00:21:34,359 --> 00:21:38,682
By noon he had passed three pine trees.

329
00:21:38,952 --> 00:21:41,323
By sunset, a fourth.

330
00:21:43,063 --> 00:21:46,314
The next day he reached the high meadows.

331
00:21:46,644 --> 00:21:49,602
Pink azaleas on every slope.

332
00:21:49,932 --> 00:21:52,829
A stream hopping over stones.

333
00:21:53,639 --> 00:21:55,025
Pink flowers!

334
00:21:55,295 --> 00:21:56,687
On the ground!

335
00:21:56,957 --> 00:21:59,996
Nobody at the palace will believe this.

336
00:22:00,746 --> 00:22:03,577
He took out the portrait to check.

337
00:22:03,847 --> 00:22:05,901
It felt a little damp.

338
00:22:06,171 --> 00:22:08,777
He did not look closely.

339
00:22:09,047 --> 00:22:09,947
He should have.

340
00:22:10,697 --> 00:22:11,806
Long ears.

341
00:22:12,076 --> 00:22:14,372
A cotton tail.

342
00:22:14,642 --> 00:22:19,213
Somewhere up here there's a rabbit, and I will find him.

343
00:22:19,963 --> 00:22:22,980
Then he stopped walking.

344
00:22:23,460 --> 00:22:27,696
Because he remembered what would happen when he did.

345
00:22:28,656 --> 00:22:33,195
And then I'll take him home to the King.

346
00:22:44,155 --> 00:22:47,867
Meanwhile, high on a hill covered in clover,

347
00:22:47,867 --> 00:22:50,650
the animals held a spring picnic.

348
00:22:51,190 --> 00:22:54,912
There was one big flat rock under the old shade tree.

349
00:22:55,182 --> 00:22:57,295
The seat of honor.

350
00:22:57,565 --> 00:22:59,161
Three animals wanted it.

351
00:22:59,911 --> 00:23:02,379
I am the eldest.

352
00:23:02,649 --> 00:23:06,688
My antlers are older than that big old tree.

353
00:23:07,438 --> 00:23:10,095
You don't have antlers, dear.

354
00:23:10,845 --> 00:23:14,156
My husband's antlers, then.

355
00:23:14,426 --> 00:23:15,980
Same thing.

356
00:23:16,730 --> 00:23:17,106
Pah!

357
00:23:17,106 --> 00:23:21,149
I dug the very first hole on this mountain.

358
00:23:21,419 --> 00:23:24,539
I'm the eldest!

359
00:23:25,289 --> 00:23:33,078
I remember when this mountain was a little hill.

360
00:23:33,408 --> 00:23:35,524
I'm the eldest.

361
00:23:49,164 --> 00:23:52,314
♪ Who's the oldest? Who's the oldest?

362
00:23:52,364 --> 00:23:56,414
♪ Who gets the seat by the old shade tree?

363
00:23:56,464 --> 00:24:00,314
♪ (Not you! Not you! That seat's for me!)

364
00:24:00,364 --> 00:24:03,414
♪ When I was a fawn, the moon was new,

365
00:24:03,464 --> 00:24:07,114
♪ The rivers were only a drop of dew,

366
00:24:07,164 --> 00:24:11,424
♪ I taught the very first rain to fall,

367
00:24:11,804 --> 00:24:14,114
♪ (Oh, here she goes again, y'all!)

368
00:24:14,164 --> 00:24:17,414
♪ I dug the valleys with my snout,

369
00:24:17,464 --> 00:24:20,414
♪ I pushed the mountains in and out,

370
00:24:20,464 --> 00:24:22,614
♪ Before me there was only mud,

371
00:24:22,664 --> 00:24:25,614
♪ (And look at you, still covered, bud!)

372
00:24:25,664 --> 00:24:29,214
♪ Who's the oldest? Who's the oldest?

373
00:24:29,264 --> 00:24:33,014
♪ Who gets the seat by the old shade tree?

374
00:24:33,064 --> 00:24:37,954
♪ (Not you! Not you! That seat's for me!)

375
00:24:38,064 --> 00:24:41,374
♪ I sat right here when this great hill

376
00:24:41,864 --> 00:24:44,814
♪ Was just a pebble, small and still,

377
00:24:44,864 --> 00:24:48,904
♪ I watched it grow up whisker-high,

378
00:24:50,464 --> 00:24:55,154
♪ (He slept right through it! Oh my, oh my!)

379
00:24:56,464 --> 00:24:58,114
♪ I'm older!

380
00:24:58,164 --> 00:25:00,174
♪ No, I'm older!

381
00:25:03,084 --> 00:25:04,414
♪ I'm the oldest!

382
00:25:04,464 --> 00:25:07,384
♪ (Now who's the boldest?)

383
00:25:07,964 --> 00:25:09,864
♪ (Eolssigu!)

384
00:25:10,564 --> 00:25:13,614
♪ Who's the oldest? Who's the oldest?

385
00:25:13,664 --> 00:25:17,414
♪ Who gets the seat by the old shade tree?

386
00:25:17,464 --> 00:25:22,154
♪ (Not you! Not you! That seat's for me!)

387
00:25:24,694 --> 00:25:26,380
Oh, dear.

388
00:25:26,650 --> 00:25:28,476
Oh, dear, dear.

389
00:25:28,746 --> 00:25:30,279
You're all babies.

390
00:25:30,759 --> 00:25:33,610
When they hung the sky, who held the ladder?

391
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:34,195
Me.

392
00:25:34,195 --> 00:25:36,720
Who handed up the stars?

393
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:37,036
Me.

394
00:25:37,786 --> 00:25:39,843
That's a lie.

395
00:25:40,713 --> 00:25:42,072
Prove it.

396
00:25:42,882 --> 00:25:43,792
They couldn't.

397
00:25:44,062 --> 00:25:48,274
So Clover the rabbit sat down on the seat of honor.

398
00:25:48,544 --> 00:25:50,093
As usual.

399
00:25:51,833 --> 00:25:56,727
Just then, puffing and very slow, a stranger arrived.

400
00:25:56,997 --> 00:25:59,821
He had been climbing for a day and a half.

401
00:26:00,571 --> 00:26:01,802
Excuse me.

402
00:26:02,072 --> 00:26:03,152
Good morning.

403
00:26:03,422 --> 00:26:07,153
Has anyone here seen this creature?

404
00:26:07,903 --> 00:26:10,699
But the sea had soaked the painting.

405
00:26:11,089 --> 00:26:14,186
The ears had run into stripes.

406
00:26:14,576 --> 00:26:17,967
The nose had run into fangs.

407
00:26:18,837 --> 00:26:20,271
It's him!

408
00:26:20,601 --> 00:26:22,963
Stripes and fangs!

409
00:26:23,773 --> 00:26:25,247
That's the tiger!

410
00:26:25,667 --> 00:26:28,595
He's looking for the tiger!

411
00:26:29,495 --> 00:26:30,808
Tiger?

412
00:26:30,808 --> 00:26:32,340
No, no.

413
00:26:32,670 --> 00:26:33,507
It's a rab-

414
00:26:34,797 --> 00:26:39,440
And from high up the valley came a voice like a landslide.

415
00:26:52,380 --> 00:26:54,186
Down the valley he came.

416
00:26:54,576 --> 00:26:56,597
Soft paws.

417
00:26:56,987 --> 00:26:58,743
Slow steps.

418
00:26:59,133 --> 00:27:01,984
Not one ant crushed.

419
00:27:02,854 --> 00:27:06,107
who is looking for me?

420
00:27:07,997 --> 00:27:09,915
Big Stripes.

421
00:27:10,185 --> 00:27:12,516
The King of the Mountain.

422
00:27:12,786 --> 00:27:14,392
In his own opinion.

423
00:27:15,142 --> 00:27:18,333
Somebody has a portrait of me?

424
00:27:18,603 --> 00:27:21,036
Oh, it's a good likeness.

425
00:27:21,306 --> 00:27:22,639
A little wet.

426
00:27:29,019 --> 00:27:32,279
♪ (Shh! Shh! Something's in the pines!)

427
00:27:35,119 --> 00:27:39,369
♪ Claws like iron sickles, and a tail as long as a pole,

428
00:27:39,419 --> 00:27:44,169
♪ Stripes like a painted screen from my whiskers to my soul,

429
00:27:44,219 --> 00:27:49,169
♪ My front legs are like pillars and my back legs like a drum,

430
00:27:49,219 --> 00:27:54,809
♪ I tiptoe down so softly not an ant knows I have come!

431
00:27:55,819 --> 00:28:00,669
♪ Make way, make way, for the King of the Mountain!

432
00:28:00,719 --> 00:28:04,569
♪ Bow down low to the best-dressed cat around!

433
00:28:04,619 --> 00:28:07,769
♪ (Hide your tails! Hide your ears!)

434
00:28:07,819 --> 00:28:09,709
♪ (Eolssigu!)

435
00:28:16,219 --> 00:28:20,969
♪ The deer all faint, the boars all run, the rabbits hide their ears,

436
00:28:21,019 --> 00:28:25,469
♪ The magpies laugh behind my back, but who cares about their jeers?

437
00:28:25,519 --> 00:28:30,239
♪ I roar one roar, the pine trees bow, the rivers change their course,

438
00:28:30,289 --> 00:28:31,769
♪ (Has he ever tried it?)

439
00:28:31,819 --> 00:28:35,189
♪ Well, not yet. But of course!

440
00:28:35,319 --> 00:28:40,239
♪ Look at me, look at me, handsome as a painting,

441
00:28:40,619 --> 00:28:44,879
♪ Somebody fan me, I think I'm fainting…

442
00:28:46,219 --> 00:28:51,069
♪ Make way, make way, for the King of the Mountain!

443
00:28:51,119 --> 00:28:54,869
♪ Bow down low to the best-dressed cat around!

444
00:28:54,919 --> 00:28:58,269
♪ (Hide your tails! Hide your ears!)

445
00:28:58,319 --> 00:29:00,209
♪ (Eolssigu!)

446
00:29:03,009 --> 00:29:09,439
♪ (Jota!)

447
00:29:14,359 --> 00:29:16,429
And what are you?

448
00:29:16,699 --> 00:29:19,614
A rock with a head?

449
00:29:19,884 --> 00:29:22,671
A dumpling with legs?

450
00:29:23,421 --> 00:29:28,890
I am Lord Terrapin, of the Dragon King's court.

451
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:35,025
Never heard of him.

452
00:29:35,355 --> 00:29:37,572
But I'm hungry.

453
00:29:37,902 --> 00:29:41,788
Terrapin soup!

454
00:29:42,598 --> 00:29:45,694
Steady pulled his head into his shell.

455
00:29:46,084 --> 00:29:47,675
Everything went dark.

456
00:29:48,545 --> 00:29:49,184
Bite.

457
00:29:49,184 --> 00:29:50,845
Never let go.

458
00:29:51,175 --> 00:29:51,814
Bite.

459
00:29:51,814 --> 00:29:53,475
Never let go.

460
00:29:54,285 --> 00:29:55,109
Hello?

461
00:29:55,109 --> 00:29:57,442
Anybody in there?

462
00:29:57,712 --> 00:30:00,483
Come out, little dumpling.

463
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:02,375
snap!

464
00:30:02,375 --> 00:30:05,044
Right on the nose!

465
00:30:05,944 --> 00:30:07,047
ow!

466
00:30:07,047 --> 00:30:10,355
ow ow ow!

467
00:30:10,775 --> 00:30:12,439
Let go!

468
00:30:12,859 --> 00:30:14,522
Let go!

469
00:30:15,422 --> 00:30:17,372
"Mm-mm," said Steady.

470
00:30:17,642 --> 00:30:19,596
He did not let go.

471
00:30:20,346 --> 00:30:23,507
who are you?

472
00:30:24,557 --> 00:30:28,968
"Mm the Dragon King's tiger-biting general.

473
00:30:29,238 --> 00:30:31,735
Mm have fifty brothers."

474
00:30:32,485 --> 00:30:33,608
mother!

475
00:30:34,658 --> 00:30:38,999
And the King of the Mountain ran all the way home.

476
00:30:39,269 --> 00:30:42,863
Steady fell on his back, legs waving.

477
00:30:44,603 --> 00:30:46,595
You bit a tiger.

478
00:30:46,925 --> 00:30:47,835
On the nose.

479
00:30:48,165 --> 00:30:50,732
I saw it with both eyes!

480
00:30:51,542 --> 00:30:52,788
Is he gone?

481
00:30:53,058 --> 00:30:55,159
I can't see.

482
00:30:55,429 --> 00:30:57,381
I'm upside down.

483
00:30:58,131 --> 00:31:02,556
Clover pushed with all his might, and flipped him over.

484
00:31:03,306 --> 00:31:09,047
Friend, you are the bravest rock with a head I ever met.

485
00:31:09,857 --> 00:31:12,188
Long ears.

486
00:31:12,518 --> 00:31:14,498
Red eyes.

487
00:31:14,828 --> 00:31:17,632
A tail like cotton.

488
00:31:17,962 --> 00:31:20,809
You're a rabbit.

489
00:31:21,619 --> 00:31:23,051
Last time I looked.

490
00:31:23,801 --> 00:31:24,724
I found him.

491
00:31:37,464 --> 00:31:41,355
That evening, the two of them sat together on the seat of honor.

492
00:31:41,685 --> 00:31:43,656
It was big enough for two.

493
00:31:44,466 --> 00:31:48,855
You told them you held the ladder when they hung the sky.

494
00:31:49,125 --> 00:31:50,819
Was that true?

495
00:31:51,569 --> 00:31:53,621
Of course not!

496
00:31:53,951 --> 00:31:57,754
Rabbits talk fast, so nobody notices we're scared.

497
00:31:58,294 --> 00:31:59,527
Hawks up there.

498
00:32:00,007 --> 00:32:03,443
Foxes down here.

499
00:32:03,923 --> 00:32:07,078
Hunters with dogs every autumn.

500
00:32:07,768 --> 00:32:11,212
I've never slept a whole night in my life.

501
00:32:11,692 --> 00:32:13,306
One ear is always up.

502
00:32:14,266 --> 00:32:16,372
That sounds lonely.

503
00:32:17,182 --> 00:32:18,045
Lonely?

504
00:32:18,315 --> 00:32:18,631
Me?

505
00:32:18,631 --> 00:32:21,903
I'm the eldest on the mountain!

506
00:32:22,173 --> 00:32:23,689
Everybody knows me!

507
00:32:24,169 --> 00:32:25,201
They know me.

508
00:32:25,681 --> 00:32:29,549
They just run away with me, or after me.

509
00:32:30,029 --> 00:32:31,828
Nobody ever stays.

510
00:32:42,918 --> 00:32:46,968
♪ Hawk in the morning, fox in the night,

511
00:32:47,018 --> 00:32:50,568
♪ Hunters at harvest with their dogs in sight,

512
00:32:50,618 --> 00:32:54,168
♪ I talk so fast and I jump so high,

513
00:32:54,218 --> 00:32:57,868
♪ Nobody sees the fear in my eye.

514
00:32:57,918 --> 00:33:01,568
♪ Always running, always running,

515
00:33:01,618 --> 00:33:05,068
♪ One ear up and one foot on the ground,

516
00:33:05,118 --> 00:33:09,048
♪ Always running, always running,

517
00:33:09,118 --> 00:33:13,048
♪ Never once have I turned around.

518
00:33:15,518 --> 00:33:19,068
♪ They say I'm the oldest, the cleverest one,

519
00:33:19,118 --> 00:33:22,768
♪ The rabbit who helped hang the moon and sun,

520
00:33:22,818 --> 00:33:26,368
♪ But who is there when the night comes down?

521
00:33:26,418 --> 00:33:30,898
♪ Who stays when the danger's all around?

522
00:33:33,718 --> 00:33:37,468
♪ Four little leaves on a clover hill,

523
00:33:37,518 --> 00:33:41,448
♪ Happy where my feet stand still.

524
00:33:44,418 --> 00:33:48,168
♪ Just once I'd like to close both eyes

525
00:33:48,218 --> 00:33:51,368
♪ And sleep until the sun can rise,

526
00:33:51,418 --> 00:33:55,168
♪ With someone near who won't run away,

527
00:33:55,218 --> 00:33:58,868
♪ Someone who'll stay… someone who'll stay.

528
00:33:58,918 --> 00:34:02,668
♪ Always running, always running,

529
00:34:02,718 --> 00:34:06,168
♪ One ear up and one foot on the ground,

530
00:34:06,218 --> 00:34:09,768
♪ Always running, always running,

531
00:34:09,818 --> 00:34:13,168
♪ Never once have I turned around.

532
00:34:13,218 --> 00:34:17,068
♪ Four little leaves on a clover hill,

533
00:34:17,118 --> 00:34:21,048
♪ Happy where my feet stand still.

534
00:34:24,918 --> 00:34:27,508
♪ Someday… someday.

535
00:34:36,138 --> 00:34:40,007
Steady looked at this funny, frightened rabbit.

536
00:34:40,397 --> 00:34:43,463
And then he thought of his sick king.

537
00:34:44,333 --> 00:34:45,222
Forgive me.

538
00:34:47,022 --> 00:34:50,746
Where I come from, there are no hawks.

539
00:34:51,016 --> 00:34:52,454
No foxes.

540
00:34:52,724 --> 00:34:54,245
No hunters.

541
00:34:54,995 --> 00:34:55,548
None?

542
00:34:55,548 --> 00:34:58,096
Not even one tiny hawk?

543
00:34:58,906 --> 00:35:00,306
Not one.

544
00:35:00,576 --> 00:35:04,662
And the Dragon King himself wants to meet you.

545
00:35:04,932 --> 00:35:06,214
Very much.

546
00:35:06,964 --> 00:35:08,743
Every word of it was true.

547
00:35:09,073 --> 00:35:11,566
That was the terrible part.

548
00:35:12,376 --> 00:35:14,242
A king wants to meet me?

549
00:35:26,122 --> 00:35:31,972
♪ There's a palace under the sea with a roof of tiles so blue,

550
00:35:32,022 --> 00:35:37,372
♪ And lanterns made of pearl that glow the whole night through,

551
00:35:37,422 --> 00:35:38,472
♪ Are there hawks?

552
00:35:38,522 --> 00:35:39,672
♪ Not a single one.

553
00:35:39,722 --> 00:35:40,772
♪ And foxes?

554
00:35:40,822 --> 00:35:42,172
♪ Not a one.

555
00:35:42,222 --> 00:35:48,372
♪ The palace under the sea, the palace under the sea,

556
00:35:48,422 --> 00:35:51,372
♪ Where nobody chases anybody,

557
00:35:51,422 --> 00:35:54,372
♪ The palace under the sea!

558
00:35:54,422 --> 00:35:59,072
♪ The King himself would like to meet you at his door,

559
00:35:59,122 --> 00:36:04,122
♪ He wants to meet you, Clover, more than anyone before,

560
00:36:04,222 --> 00:36:06,722
♪ Me? A rabbit with a crooked ear?

561
00:36:06,722 --> 00:36:09,122
♪ The King of all the sea wants me down there?

562
00:36:09,222 --> 00:36:12,022
♪ A seat of honor, a pillow of silk,

563
00:36:12,222 --> 00:36:14,872
♪ Seaweed cakes and a cup of milk,

564
00:36:14,922 --> 00:36:20,222
♪ And sleep, a whole night through, with both my ears laid down!

565
00:36:24,722 --> 00:36:27,322
♪ Every word I say is true,

566
00:36:29,222 --> 00:36:32,722
♪ Then why does my heart feel heavy too?

567
00:36:37,522 --> 00:36:43,672
♪ The palace under the sea, the palace under the sea,

568
00:36:43,722 --> 00:36:46,772
♪ Where nobody chases anybody,

569
00:36:46,822 --> 00:36:50,082
♪ The palace under the sea!

570
00:36:52,592 --> 00:36:53,069
Wait.

571
00:36:53,069 --> 00:36:54,690
What's the catch?

572
00:36:55,080 --> 00:36:56,771
There's always a catch.

573
00:36:57,641 --> 00:37:00,732
Steady opened his mouth.

574
00:37:01,122 --> 00:37:05,156
He had never told a lie in his life.

575
00:37:06,026 --> 00:37:10,457
The King needs a very important guest.

576
00:37:10,847 --> 00:37:14,913
You would be the most important one.

577
00:37:15,783 --> 00:37:16,620
Important.

578
00:37:16,890 --> 00:37:17,153
Me.

579
00:37:17,153 --> 00:37:19,956
A rabbit could get used to that.

580
00:37:20,436 --> 00:37:23,007
There's just one thing.

581
00:37:23,397 --> 00:37:24,765
I can't swim.

582
00:37:25,635 --> 00:37:27,386
Hold on to my shell.

583
00:37:27,716 --> 00:37:29,438
I won't let you fall.

584
00:37:42,388 --> 00:37:47,834
At sunrise, a rabbit rode out to sea on the back of a terrapin.

585
00:37:48,104 --> 00:37:49,671
Screaming.

586
00:37:50,151 --> 00:37:53,631
Clover squealed at every single wave.

587
00:37:53,901 --> 00:37:59,558
Steady calmly explained that wet was the main thing about the sea.

588
00:38:00,038 --> 00:38:06,929
A big wave lifted them up, and dropped them down, and lifted them up again.

589
00:38:08,669 --> 00:38:14,360
Halfway across, they rested on a little rock with one bent pine tree.

590
00:38:15,170 --> 00:38:20,762
That was wonderful!

591
00:38:21,092 --> 00:38:24,020
The going up, and the coming down!

592
00:38:24,350 --> 00:38:26,266
Do it again!

593
00:38:26,806 --> 00:38:29,817
Steady, have you ever laughed?

594
00:38:30,087 --> 00:38:31,485
Even once?

595
00:38:31,755 --> 00:38:32,368
Try it.

596
00:38:32,638 --> 00:38:34,379
Say whee.

597
00:38:35,129 --> 00:38:36,400
Whee.

598
00:38:37,150 --> 00:38:38,540
With your heart!

599
00:38:39,350 --> 00:38:40,708
Whee!

600
00:38:40,708 --> 00:38:41,523
Ha!

601
00:38:41,853 --> 00:38:44,891
Ha ha ha!

602
00:38:45,701 --> 00:38:50,553
Nobody in the Southern Sea had ever heard the terrapin laugh.

603
00:38:50,883 --> 00:38:52,806
Not even the terrapin.

604
00:38:53,616 --> 00:38:56,908
You know, you're the first one who ever carried me.

605
00:38:57,238 --> 00:38:59,152
Everyone else just chases me.

606
00:38:59,962 --> 00:39:03,926
Steady's heart turned over inside his shell.

607
00:39:04,796 --> 00:39:05,687
Clover.

608
00:39:06,077 --> 00:39:08,607
There's something I have to tell you.

609
00:39:08,997 --> 00:39:11,311
About the King.

610
00:39:11,311 --> 00:39:12,237
He is-

611
00:39:13,107 --> 00:39:13,737
Look!

612
00:39:13,737 --> 00:39:14,745
A whale!

613
00:39:15,075 --> 00:39:16,449
He's waving at us!

614
00:39:16,779 --> 00:39:18,024
Hello, whale!

615
00:39:18,834 --> 00:39:20,929
And the moment was gone.

616
00:39:35,379 --> 00:39:38,929
♪ The waves go up, the waves go down,

617
00:39:38,979 --> 00:39:42,429
♪ The gulls fly high, the sun's a crown,

618
00:39:42,479 --> 00:39:45,829
♪ I've never been this far from home,

619
00:39:45,879 --> 00:39:48,529
♪ With nothing below but blue and foam.

620
00:39:48,579 --> 00:39:54,229
♪ Hold on to my shell, hold on to my shell,

621
00:39:54,279 --> 00:39:59,179
♪ I won't let you fall, I won't let you fall.

622
00:40:01,179 --> 00:40:04,829
♪ I'm not very fast and I'm not very tall,

623
00:40:04,879 --> 00:40:08,129
♪ I'm hardly a hero at all, at all,

624
00:40:08,179 --> 00:40:11,029
♪ But I've got a back that is broad and strong,

625
00:40:11,079 --> 00:40:14,629
♪ And a heart that can carry you all night long.

626
00:40:14,679 --> 00:40:17,529
♪ Everyone else just chased me down,

627
00:40:17,579 --> 00:40:20,829
♪ The fox, the hawk, the hounds from town,

628
00:40:20,879 --> 00:40:24,029
♪ You're the first who ever carried me,

629
00:40:24,079 --> 00:40:28,449
♪ Who knew a friend was a rock in the sea?

630
00:40:35,779 --> 00:40:40,149
♪ Oh, if he knew where this road will end,

631
00:40:42,879 --> 00:40:46,919
♪ Would he still call me his friend?

632
00:40:48,479 --> 00:40:54,129
♪ Hold on to my shell, hold on to my shell,

633
00:40:54,179 --> 00:40:59,079
♪ I won't let you fall, I won't let you fall.

634
00:41:00,179 --> 00:41:01,559
♪ Whee!

635
00:41:09,109 --> 00:41:11,881
Then Steady dived.

636
00:41:12,271 --> 00:41:17,883
Down, down, into the deep blue, where the sunlight gives up.

637
00:41:18,483 --> 00:41:22,892
Against his shell, Steady could feel the rabbit's heart.

638
00:41:23,222 --> 00:41:24,628
Beating fast.

639
00:41:24,958 --> 00:41:26,636
So fast.

640
00:41:27,176 --> 00:41:31,628
He swam a little slower, and held a little steadier.

641
00:41:31,958 --> 00:41:34,835
He did not let him fall.

642
00:41:50,385 --> 00:41:51,516
Horns blew.

643
00:41:51,846 --> 00:41:54,022
Drums boomed.

644
00:41:54,352 --> 00:41:58,122
Rows of crab soldiers raised their spears.

645
00:41:58,932 --> 00:41:59,809
A parade?

646
00:42:00,139 --> 00:42:01,070
For me?

647
00:42:01,400 --> 00:42:04,839
Steady, you didn't say there'd be a parade!

648
00:42:05,649 --> 00:42:09,683
Welcome, welcome, honored guest!

649
00:42:09,953 --> 00:42:11,129
Come in!

650
00:42:11,399 --> 00:42:12,576
Come in!

651
00:42:12,846 --> 00:42:14,732
Mind the door!

652
00:42:15,482 --> 00:42:20,040
Steady walked beside his friend and said nothing at all.

653
00:42:21,990 --> 00:42:22,413
So.

654
00:42:22,413 --> 00:42:24,808
This is a rabbit.

655
00:42:25,078 --> 00:42:28,960
Lord Terrapin, is this the one?

656
00:42:29,710 --> 00:42:31,414
Yes, Majesty.

657
00:42:32,374 --> 00:42:33,589
Your Majesty!

658
00:42:33,859 --> 00:42:36,003
Clover of Clover Hill.

659
00:42:36,273 --> 00:42:37,364
Delighted.

660
00:42:37,634 --> 00:42:40,576
Now, about my seat of honor-

661
00:42:41,326 --> 00:42:43,243
Seize him!

662
00:42:44,143 --> 00:42:47,289
Crab claws snapped shut.

663
00:42:47,679 --> 00:42:50,062
Kelp ropes wound tight.

664
00:42:50,452 --> 00:42:54,842
In one breath, the honored guest was a prisoner.

665
00:42:55,712 --> 00:42:57,026
What is this?

666
00:42:57,356 --> 00:42:58,287
What did I do?

667
00:42:59,097 --> 00:43:03,716
The cure for my sickness is inside that rabbit.

668
00:43:03,986 --> 00:43:06,830
Doctor, you may begin.

669
00:43:07,580 --> 00:43:10,598
Hold still, little one.

670
00:43:10,988 --> 00:43:13,415
It's only your liver.

671
00:43:13,805 --> 00:43:18,847
The King cannot wait.

672
00:43:19,717 --> 00:43:20,760
Steady.

673
00:43:21,330 --> 00:43:23,388
Look at me.

674
00:43:23,958 --> 00:43:28,129
You said we were friends.

675
00:43:29,179 --> 00:43:29,588
Yes.

676
00:43:29,588 --> 00:43:33,366
The moment you saw at the very start.

677
00:43:33,846 --> 00:43:37,415
Steady could not say a single word.

678
00:43:38,905 --> 00:43:42,516
But the fastest thing about a rabbit is not his feet.

679
00:43:42,906 --> 00:43:44,533
It's his mouth.

680
00:43:45,403 --> 00:43:45,975
Ha!

681
00:43:45,975 --> 00:43:47,694
Ha ha ha!

682
00:43:48,024 --> 00:43:51,134
Oh, Majesty.

683
00:43:51,464 --> 00:43:54,464
You poor, poor king.

684
00:43:55,274 --> 00:43:57,747
Why is it laughing?

685
00:43:58,557 --> 00:44:00,247
My liver?

686
00:44:00,517 --> 00:44:01,715
It's not in here.

687
00:44:01,985 --> 00:44:03,567
I left it at home.

688
00:44:14,947 --> 00:44:16,747
♪ Oh, Majesty, dear Majesty, I'd give it with a smile,

689
00:44:16,747 --> 00:44:18,547
♪ A rabbit's liver cures a king, it's famous, mile on mile!

690
00:44:18,547 --> 00:44:20,447
♪ But every rabbit knows a thing your doctor never read,

691
00:44:20,447 --> 00:44:22,247
♪ We never keep our livers in!

692
00:44:22,247 --> 00:44:24,747
♪ (He never keeps it in?)

693
00:44:25,847 --> 00:44:29,447
♪ One small thing, Your Majesty, one small thing,

694
00:44:29,447 --> 00:44:33,147
♪ It's hanging on a pine by a mountain spring!

695
00:44:33,147 --> 00:44:35,647
♪ (A pine by a spring? A pine by a spring!)

696
00:44:36,747 --> 00:44:38,547
♪ Each morning when the sun comes up, we take our livers out,

697
00:44:38,547 --> 00:44:40,447
♪ We wash them in the silver stream and swish them all about,

698
00:44:40,447 --> 00:44:42,247
♪ We hang them on a pine tree branch to dry in the fresh air,

699
00:44:42,247 --> 00:44:44,047
♪ And that's where mine is swinging now!

700
00:44:44,047 --> 00:44:45,847
♪ (It's where?)

701
00:44:45,847 --> 00:44:47,647
♪ Up there!

702
00:44:47,647 --> 00:44:49,547
♪ If only your good terrapin had told me what you need,

703
00:44:49,547 --> 00:44:51,347
♪ I would have packed it with my lunch and brought it here at speed!

704
00:44:51,347 --> 00:44:54,947
♪ Is this the truth, you rabbit?

705
00:44:54,947 --> 00:44:58,657
♪ Upon my ears, it's true!

706
00:45:09,547 --> 00:45:12,047
♪ (Can a rabbit? Could a rabbit? Would a rabbit? Should a rabbit?)

707
00:45:13,147 --> 00:45:14,947
♪ (Eolssigu!)

708
00:45:14,947 --> 00:45:18,547
♪ One small thing, Your Majesty, one small thing,

709
00:45:18,547 --> 00:45:22,247
♪ It's hanging on a pine by a mountain spring!

710
00:45:22,247 --> 00:45:24,747
♪ (A pine by a spring? A pine by a spring!)

711
00:45:25,847 --> 00:45:29,547
♪ So send me home, Your Majesty, I'll be back by noon!

712
00:45:29,547 --> 00:45:31,347
♪ (With the liver?)

713
00:45:31,347 --> 00:45:35,347
♪ With the liver! And a spoon!

714
00:45:47,247 --> 00:45:48,916
Doctor!

715
00:45:49,306 --> 00:45:53,669
Can a rabbit really take out its own liver?

716
00:45:54,539 --> 00:45:55,284
Hmm.

717
00:45:55,284 --> 00:45:56,774
Hmm-hmm.

718
00:45:57,044 --> 00:45:59,390
The book doesn't say it can't.

719
00:46:00,140 --> 00:46:02,160
Lord Terrapin.

720
00:46:02,430 --> 00:46:04,326
You traveled with him.

721
00:46:04,596 --> 00:46:08,831
You are the one creature here who never lies.

722
00:46:09,311 --> 00:46:10,945
Is it true?

723
00:46:11,695 --> 00:46:14,379
Clover looked at Steady.

724
00:46:14,769 --> 00:46:16,777
Steady looked at his king.

725
00:46:17,377 --> 00:46:21,883
He felt that rabbit's heart beating on his shell,

726
00:46:21,883 --> 00:46:24,366
all the way across the sea.

727
00:46:25,876 --> 00:46:27,871
It is true, Majesty.

728
00:46:28,621 --> 00:46:32,582
It was the first lie Steady had ever told.

729
00:46:33,542 --> 00:46:35,274
Then go!

730
00:46:35,694 --> 00:46:36,721
Both of you!

731
00:46:37,141 --> 00:46:41,011
Go back at once and fetch that liver!

732
00:46:41,911 --> 00:46:42,406
Phew.

733
00:46:53,856 --> 00:46:57,574
All the way back, neither of them said a word.

734
00:46:58,054 --> 00:46:59,689
No whale waved.

735
00:47:01,639 --> 00:47:04,527
But the moment his feet touched sand,

736
00:47:04,527 --> 00:47:07,570
Clover leaped off and ran up the beach!

737
00:47:08,320 --> 00:47:08,656
Ha!

738
00:47:08,656 --> 00:47:11,231
A liver on a pine tree!

739
00:47:11,561 --> 00:47:14,172
Who takes out his own liver?

740
00:47:14,502 --> 00:47:16,872
You fish-brained fools!

741
00:47:27,312 --> 00:47:30,762
♪ Silly old terrapin, slow old shell,

742
00:47:30,812 --> 00:47:33,662
♪ Who takes out a liver? Couldn't you tell?

743
00:47:33,712 --> 00:47:37,362
♪ It's in my tummy where it's always been,

744
00:47:37,412 --> 00:47:40,962
♪ Right where a liver is meant to be in!

745
00:47:41,012 --> 00:47:44,862
♪ Catch me if you can, catch me if you can,

746
00:47:44,912 --> 00:47:50,212
♪ Hop, hop, hop to the mountain, catch me if you can!

747
00:47:50,412 --> 00:47:52,312
♪ (Eolssigu!)

748
00:47:53,212 --> 00:47:56,452
♪ Tell your king with his fishy crown

749
00:47:56,502 --> 00:47:59,962
♪ To hang his liver on a pine upside down,

750
00:48:00,012 --> 00:48:03,612
♪ And tell the doctor with his whiskers grey,

751
00:48:03,662 --> 00:48:07,262
♪ Next time read the whole book through, okay?

752
00:48:07,312 --> 00:48:10,962
♪ A rabbit's mouth is faster than a rabbit's feet,

753
00:48:11,012 --> 00:48:15,162
♪ And a rabbit's feet are faster than anything you'll meet!

754
00:48:15,212 --> 00:48:19,162
♪ Catch me if you can, catch me if you can,

755
00:48:19,212 --> 00:48:24,412
♪ Hop, hop, hop to the mountain, catch me if you can!

756
00:48:24,712 --> 00:48:26,612
♪ (Eolssigu!)

757
00:48:33,212 --> 00:48:37,262
♪ Catch me if you can, catch me if you can,

758
00:48:37,312 --> 00:48:41,962
♪ Hop, hop, hop to the mountain, catch me if you can!

759
00:48:42,012 --> 00:48:43,162
♪ (Eolssigu!)

760
00:48:43,212 --> 00:48:45,802
♪ So long, slowpoke! Ha, ha, ha!

761
00:48:49,822 --> 00:48:52,607
So long, you slow old rock!

762
00:48:52,877 --> 00:48:55,738
Tell your king to try seaweed!

763
00:48:56,488 --> 00:48:57,224
I know.

764
00:48:57,974 --> 00:48:58,645
You know?

765
00:48:58,975 --> 00:48:59,968
You know what?

766
00:49:00,778 --> 00:49:04,599
I carried you across the whole sea.

767
00:49:04,929 --> 00:49:08,536
Your heart was beating on my back the entire way.

768
00:49:09,076 --> 00:49:13,429
And a liver sits right next to the heart.

769
00:49:13,699 --> 00:49:15,791
You had it with you all along.

770
00:49:16,541 --> 00:49:19,567
Then why did you tell your king it was true?

771
00:49:20,437 --> 00:49:23,747
Because you said we were friends.

772
00:49:24,557 --> 00:49:30,150
For once in his life, the fastest mouth on the mountain had nothing to say.

773
00:49:31,110 --> 00:49:32,561
You lied.

774
00:49:33,131 --> 00:49:35,142
To your own king.

775
00:49:35,712 --> 00:49:36,883
For me.

776
00:49:37,933 --> 00:49:39,643
First time in my life.

777
00:49:39,913 --> 00:49:42,820
It tasted like old seaweed.

778
00:49:43,570 --> 00:49:44,857
Then don't go back!

779
00:49:45,247 --> 00:49:46,502
Stay here!

780
00:49:46,892 --> 00:49:48,406
Clover Hill has room.

781
00:49:48,796 --> 00:49:50,833
I'll share the seat of honor!

782
00:49:51,703 --> 00:49:54,302
My king is still sick.

783
00:49:54,572 --> 00:49:57,593
And my feet belong in the sea.

784
00:49:57,863 --> 00:50:00,102
I have to tell him the truth.

785
00:50:00,852 --> 00:50:02,782
They'll punish you!

786
00:50:03,352 --> 00:50:06,521
That doctor has a knife!

787
00:50:07,571 --> 00:50:08,619
Probably.

788
00:50:08,949 --> 00:50:10,840
Goodbye, Clover.

789
00:50:11,170 --> 00:50:13,541
Hold on to your hill.

790
00:50:14,351 --> 00:50:17,903
And the terrapin slid into the waves.

791
00:50:18,383 --> 00:50:19,488
Slowly.

792
00:50:19,968 --> 00:50:20,938
Of course.

793
00:50:38,188 --> 00:50:42,138
♪ The water's cold on the long way down,

794
00:50:42,188 --> 00:50:45,838
♪ The light goes out where the kelp beds drown,

795
00:50:45,888 --> 00:50:49,538
♪ I told one lie, and it saved a friend,

796
00:50:49,588 --> 00:50:54,178
♪ I'll tell the truth, and I'll pay in the end.

797
00:50:55,888 --> 00:50:59,938
♪ A heavy shell, a heavy shell,

798
00:50:59,988 --> 00:51:03,538
♪ I carried a friend and I carried him well,

799
00:51:03,588 --> 00:51:07,238
♪ Now all I carry is what I must tell,

800
00:51:07,288 --> 00:51:10,098
♪ A heavy, heavy shell.

801
00:51:10,588 --> 00:51:14,138
♪ He called me a rock, he called me slow,

802
00:51:14,188 --> 00:51:17,838
♪ He's right about that, and I let him go,

803
00:51:17,888 --> 00:51:22,138
♪ He's up on his hill where the clover grows,

804
00:51:22,188 --> 00:51:26,778
♪ And that's where a rabbit belongs, I know.

805
00:51:27,488 --> 00:51:31,238
♪ Steady, steady, one flipper at a time,

806
00:51:31,288 --> 00:51:35,768
♪ Slow as the tide, but I'll get there fine.

807
00:51:40,788 --> 00:51:43,738
♪ My King once opened a net for me,

808
00:51:43,788 --> 00:51:47,138
♪ He said, "Go on, little one, swim free."

809
00:51:47,188 --> 00:51:50,138
♪ If I must answer with my shell,

810
00:51:50,188 --> 00:51:54,228
♪ Let the truth ring out like a bell.

811
00:51:58,088 --> 00:52:01,838
♪ A heavy shell, a heavy shell,

812
00:52:01,888 --> 00:52:05,538
♪ I carried a friend and I carried him well,

813
00:52:05,588 --> 00:52:09,238
♪ Now all I carry is what I must tell,

814
00:52:09,288 --> 00:52:12,098
♪ A heavy, heavy shell.

815
00:52:43,768 --> 00:52:47,237
That night, Clover was home.

816
00:52:47,567 --> 00:52:49,574
Safe on his hill.

817
00:52:49,904 --> 00:52:53,394
Sitting on the seat of honor, all alone.

818
00:52:54,204 --> 00:52:56,295
You got away, boy!

819
00:52:56,565 --> 00:52:58,182
From a king!

820
00:52:58,452 --> 00:53:01,568
Nobody on this mountain ever did that!

821
00:53:02,318 --> 00:53:06,334
We'll tell the story for a hundred years.

822
00:53:06,604 --> 00:53:07,932
Well, I will.

823
00:53:08,202 --> 00:53:09,968
I'm the eldest.

824
00:53:10,718 --> 00:53:11,436
Mm.

825
00:53:12,396 --> 00:53:14,182
You're not sleeping.

826
00:53:14,452 --> 00:53:18,833
You're not even eating clover.

827
00:53:19,103 --> 00:53:20,866
What's wrong with you?

828
00:53:21,616 --> 00:53:24,627
One ear is always up, you know.

829
00:53:25,107 --> 00:53:29,093
But tonight both ears are pointing at the sea.

830
00:53:30,053 --> 00:53:34,873
Then Clover got up, went to the roots of the old shade tree,

831
00:53:34,873 --> 00:53:36,239
and began to dig.

832
00:53:37,049 --> 00:53:38,964
Wild mountain ginseng.

833
00:53:39,294 --> 00:53:41,239
I've saved it my whole life.

834
00:53:41,569 --> 00:53:44,397
For the day I got too old to run.

835
00:53:44,937 --> 00:53:46,896
A rabbit runs away.

836
00:53:47,286 --> 00:53:48,514
That's what we do.

837
00:53:48,904 --> 00:53:50,068
Not today.

838
00:54:02,668 --> 00:54:05,668
♪ All my life I ran from the hawk,

839
00:54:05,668 --> 00:54:08,668
♪ All my life I ran from the fox,

840
00:54:08,668 --> 00:54:11,668
♪ Every rabbit knows the rule:

841
00:54:11,668 --> 00:54:14,668
♪ When there's trouble, run like a fool!

842
00:54:14,668 --> 00:54:17,668
♪ But today I'll run the other way,

843
00:54:17,668 --> 00:54:20,668
♪ Run the other way, run the other way!

844
00:54:20,668 --> 00:54:23,668
♪ Down to the sea where my friend has gone,

845
00:54:23,668 --> 00:54:26,668
♪ Run the other way till the break of dawn!

846
00:54:26,668 --> 00:54:29,168
♪ (Go on! Go on!)

847
00:54:29,668 --> 00:54:32,668
♪ Where are you going?

848
00:54:32,668 --> 00:54:35,668
♪ That way's the sea!

849
00:54:35,668 --> 00:54:38,668
♪ Rabbits can't swim!

850
00:54:38,668 --> 00:54:41,668
♪ Well, don't tell me!

851
00:54:41,668 --> 00:54:44,668
♪ I've got a root that I saved for years,

852
00:54:44,668 --> 00:54:47,668
♪ For the day I'm old with droopy ears,

853
00:54:47,668 --> 00:54:50,668
♪ But what's a treasure you never share?

854
00:54:50,668 --> 00:54:53,668
♪ A root in the ground, and nobody there.

855
00:54:53,668 --> 00:54:56,668
♪ Four little leaves on a clover hill,

856
00:54:56,668 --> 00:54:59,668
♪ Happy where my feet stand still.

857
00:54:59,668 --> 00:55:02,668
♪ But my feet won't stay, my feet won't stay,

858
00:55:02,668 --> 00:55:05,668
♪ Till they carry me to him today!

859
00:55:05,668 --> 00:55:08,168
♪ (Eolssigu!)

860
00:55:08,668 --> 00:55:11,668
♪ But today I'll run the other way,

861
00:55:11,668 --> 00:55:14,668
♪ Run the other way, run the other way!

862
00:55:14,668 --> 00:55:17,668
♪ Down to the sea where my friend has gone,

863
00:55:17,668 --> 00:55:20,668
♪ Run the other way till the break of dawn!

864
00:55:20,668 --> 00:55:23,168
♪ (Go on! Go on!)

865
00:55:23,668 --> 00:55:25,688
♪ Go on!

866
00:55:35,878 --> 00:55:41,455
At dawn, a rabbit stood at the edge of the sea, holding a root.

867
00:55:42,325 --> 00:55:43,846
I can't swim.

868
00:55:44,236 --> 00:55:45,757
I can't swim.

869
00:55:46,147 --> 00:55:49,958
I really, truly cannot swim.

870
00:55:50,558 --> 00:55:52,794
Hold on to my shell.

871
00:55:53,184 --> 00:55:55,421
Hold on to my shell.

872
00:55:56,291 --> 00:55:57,901
And he jumped!

873
00:55:58,531 --> 00:55:59,732
Splash.

874
00:56:00,002 --> 00:56:02,052
Then bubbles.

875
00:56:02,322 --> 00:56:10,280
Then, very slowly, something round came up under him.

876
00:56:11,030 --> 00:56:12,237
Clover?!

877
00:56:12,567 --> 00:56:14,387
You can't swim!

878
00:56:15,197 --> 00:56:16,502
I noticed!

879
00:56:16,982 --> 00:56:19,015
And you're still here?

880
00:56:19,285 --> 00:56:21,456
You left yesterday!

881
00:56:22,206 --> 00:56:24,469
I'm a terrapin.

882
00:56:24,739 --> 00:56:27,775
I've gone about as far as a good sneeze.

883
00:56:28,255 --> 00:56:30,036
Why did you come?

884
00:56:30,426 --> 00:56:32,218
They'll have the knife ready.

885
00:56:33,088 --> 00:56:35,119
Because you lied for me.

886
00:56:35,449 --> 00:56:38,219
Now somebody's going to tell the truth for you.

887
00:56:39,029 --> 00:56:42,231
So the terrapin swam down again.

888
00:56:42,561 --> 00:56:44,974
With his friend on his back.

889
00:56:45,304 --> 00:56:46,352
And a root.

890
00:56:46,682 --> 00:56:48,682
And no plan at all.

891
00:56:59,282 --> 00:57:04,551
Two days later, the Dragon King could hardly lift his head.

892
00:57:04,941 --> 00:57:07,450
The whole court waited.

893
00:57:08,320 --> 00:57:09,620
They're back!

894
00:57:09,890 --> 00:57:11,594
Both of them!

895
00:57:11,864 --> 00:57:13,813
Did you bring it?

896
00:57:14,083 --> 00:57:16,518
The liver on the pine tree?

897
00:57:17,268 --> 00:57:21,359
Steady bowed down until his nose touched the cold floor.

898
00:57:22,229 --> 00:57:23,415
Majesty.

899
00:57:23,685 --> 00:57:25,527
I lied to you.

900
00:57:25,797 --> 00:57:29,717
The rabbit's liver was never on land.

901
00:57:29,987 --> 00:57:32,199
It was in him all along.

902
00:57:32,679 --> 00:57:33,983
I let him go.

903
00:57:34,463 --> 00:57:37,434
Punish me, not him.

904
00:57:38,394 --> 00:57:39,882
Treason!

905
00:57:40,782 --> 00:57:43,200
And also very rude!

906
00:57:43,950 --> 00:57:44,418
You.

907
00:57:44,418 --> 00:57:49,338
The one creature in my sea who never lied.

908
00:57:50,088 --> 00:57:51,018
Majesty!

909
00:57:51,408 --> 00:57:54,763
If you want a liver, you'll have to go through me first!

910
00:57:55,363 --> 00:57:58,986
Which, fair enough, is exactly where it is.

911
00:57:59,466 --> 00:58:01,277
But I brought you something better.

912
00:58:01,607 --> 00:58:03,523
Wild mountain ginseng.

913
00:58:03,853 --> 00:58:05,525
My whole life's treasure.

914
00:58:06,335 --> 00:58:08,265
Ginseng?

915
00:58:08,595 --> 00:58:09,312
Wait.

916
00:58:09,312 --> 00:58:10,029
Wait.

917
00:58:10,569 --> 00:58:12,420
Page two.

918
00:58:12,690 --> 00:58:15,627
Wild mountain ginseng.

919
00:58:15,897 --> 00:58:22,416
Even better than a liver, actually.

920
00:58:23,166 --> 00:58:25,017
page two?!

921
00:58:25,917 --> 00:58:34,378
Nobody ever reads page two, Majesty.

922
00:58:35,128 --> 00:58:36,259
Rabbit.

923
00:58:36,529 --> 00:58:38,620
You were free.

924
00:58:38,890 --> 00:58:40,292
Why come back?

925
00:58:41,042 --> 00:58:43,508
Because he came back for me first.

926
00:58:44,318 --> 00:58:47,172
And you, Lord Terrapin.

927
00:58:47,652 --> 00:58:50,797
Why did you lie to your king?

928
00:58:51,757 --> 00:58:53,688
Because of you, Majesty.

929
00:58:54,018 --> 00:58:57,559
When I was caught in a net, you tore it open.

930
00:58:58,099 --> 00:59:00,718
You didn't ask what I was worth.

931
00:59:01,048 --> 00:59:04,481
You said: go on, little one, swim.

932
00:59:04,811 --> 00:59:07,123
I only did what you taught me.

933
00:59:07,933 --> 00:59:13,045
The Dragon King said nothing for a long, long time.

934
00:59:14,005 --> 00:59:16,404
I forgot that prince.

935
00:59:16,974 --> 00:59:23,655
I ate, and shouted, and forgot who I was.

936
00:59:24,435 --> 00:59:30,110
A servant who obeys me is loyal to my words.

937
00:59:30,440 --> 00:59:33,993
A servant who stops me is loyal to me.

938
00:59:34,803 --> 00:59:36,585
Take the ginseng, Majesty.

939
00:59:36,855 --> 00:59:38,459
Less feasting.

940
00:59:38,729 --> 00:59:40,180
More walking.

941
00:59:40,660 --> 00:59:43,093
And once a day, go up and feel the sun.

942
00:59:43,423 --> 00:59:45,426
The cure is where your feet are.

943
00:59:45,756 --> 00:59:46,648
Use them.

944
00:59:47,458 --> 00:59:49,089
Kings don't walk.

945
00:59:49,359 --> 00:59:50,306
Kings are-

946
00:59:51,056 --> 00:59:54,425
Every eye in the hall looked at him.

947
00:59:55,175 --> 00:59:57,286
Kings will learn.

948
01:00:09,526 --> 01:00:14,976
♪ I had a thousand ministers who told me I was right,

949
01:00:15,026 --> 01:00:20,476
♪ They filled my bowl, they bowed so low, they fed me day and night,

950
01:00:20,526 --> 01:00:23,376
♪ But one small voice from the back of the hall

951
01:00:23,426 --> 01:00:26,476
♪ Told me the truth, and it saved us all.

952
01:00:26,526 --> 01:00:31,976
♪ A friend tells you true, a friend tells you true,

953
01:00:32,026 --> 01:00:35,076
♪ Even when the truth is the hardest thing to do,

954
01:00:35,126 --> 01:00:37,976
♪ A friend tells you true.

955
01:00:38,026 --> 01:00:41,956
♪ I kept my word, and I broke my word,

956
01:00:43,326 --> 01:00:48,026
♪ The strangest thing that you ever heard,

957
01:00:48,526 --> 01:00:51,376
♪ But a promise to a friend and a promise to a king

958
01:00:51,426 --> 01:00:54,476
♪ Can turn out to be the very same thing.

959
01:00:54,526 --> 01:00:57,476
♪ I ran away, but I came right back,

960
01:00:57,526 --> 01:01:00,476
♪ Down through the blue on a terrapin's track,

961
01:01:00,526 --> 01:01:03,276
♪ And I found out, as I held on tight,

962
01:01:03,326 --> 01:01:07,676
♪ A friend is the one who holds on through the night.

963
01:01:07,726 --> 01:01:11,316
♪ We should have read page two!

964
01:01:13,296 --> 01:01:16,506
♪ I should have gone myself!

965
01:01:17,826 --> 01:01:21,386
♪ (Oh no, you shouldn't!)

966
01:01:22,226 --> 01:01:23,606
♪ (Jota!)

967
01:01:27,726 --> 01:01:31,546
♪ The cure is where your feet are,

968
01:01:35,426 --> 01:01:41,266
♪ Right here, right where you stand.

969
01:01:45,026 --> 01:01:50,576
♪ A friend tells you true, a friend tells you true,

970
01:01:50,626 --> 01:01:53,876
♪ Even when the truth is the hardest thing to do,

971
01:01:53,926 --> 01:01:57,076
♪ A friend tells you true.

972
01:02:14,986 --> 01:02:19,477
One month later, a very strange thing was seen on the beach.

973
01:02:19,807 --> 01:02:21,402
A dragon.

974
01:02:21,732 --> 01:02:22,452
Walking.

975
01:02:23,262 --> 01:02:25,280
Twenty steps!

976
01:02:25,550 --> 01:02:27,716
Count properly, Flounder!

977
01:02:28,466 --> 01:02:30,133
Twenty-one, Majesty.

978
01:02:30,403 --> 01:02:34,763
And please, wait for your ministers.

979
01:02:35,513 --> 01:02:38,452
His pulse is strong.

980
01:02:38,782 --> 01:02:41,045
His belly is smaller.

981
01:02:41,375 --> 01:02:45,546
And he laughs every day.

982
01:02:46,356 --> 01:02:49,782
The sun on my face.

983
01:02:50,112 --> 01:02:53,717
Why did nobody tell me about this?

984
01:02:54,527 --> 01:02:57,284
We did, Majesty.

985
01:02:57,554 --> 01:03:00,045
For forty days.

986
01:03:01,785 --> 01:03:03,008
Steady.

987
01:03:03,278 --> 01:03:08,440
From today you are my Ambassador to the Land.

988
01:03:08,710 --> 01:03:11,158
The only one I trust.

989
01:03:11,908 --> 01:03:13,904
Me, Majesty?

990
01:03:14,234 --> 01:03:17,527
I'm the slowest creature in the sea.

991
01:03:18,337 --> 01:03:19,767
Exactly.

992
01:03:20,097 --> 01:03:22,841
You always get there.

993
01:03:23,171 --> 01:03:26,332
And you tell me the truth when you do.

994
01:03:27,142 --> 01:03:28,906
Lord Ambassador!

995
01:03:29,176 --> 01:03:30,679
Can I still ride on your back?

996
01:03:31,429 --> 01:03:34,259
Hold on to my shell.

997
01:03:35,069 --> 01:03:38,697
Then a shadow fell across the sand.

998
01:03:39,087 --> 01:03:44,116
Down from the mountain came, of all things, a tiger.

999
01:03:44,986 --> 01:03:47,091
Relax, everyone!

1000
01:03:47,361 --> 01:03:51,172
I'm only here for the party!

1001
01:03:51,652 --> 01:03:56,086
And I'm standing way over here.

1002
01:03:56,476 --> 01:03:58,522
Far from him.

1003
01:03:59,392 --> 01:04:01,871
Steady opened his mouth.

1004
01:04:02,141 --> 01:04:03,578
Just a little.

1005
01:04:04,328 --> 01:04:05,021
Eep!

1006
01:04:06,821 --> 01:04:11,018
That night, land and sea threw a feast on the beach.

1007
01:04:11,348 --> 01:04:13,144
A small feast.

1008
01:04:13,474 --> 01:04:15,488
The King insisted.

1009
01:04:16,298 --> 01:04:18,449
Just one rice cake.

1010
01:04:18,719 --> 01:04:20,782
Maybe two.

1011
01:04:21,532 --> 01:04:23,063
Majesty!

1012
01:04:23,813 --> 01:04:24,766
One!

1013
01:04:25,576 --> 01:04:26,560
Up on a rock,

1014
01:04:26,560 --> 01:04:31,400
a terrapin and a rabbit watched the moon come up out of the sea.

1015
01:04:32,210 --> 01:04:34,273
So, Lord Ambassador.

1016
01:04:34,543 --> 01:04:36,062
Where's home now?

1017
01:04:36,332 --> 01:04:38,096
The sea, or the land?

1018
01:04:38,846 --> 01:04:40,791
Wherever my feet are.

1019
01:04:41,121 --> 01:04:42,892
And wherever you are.

1020
01:04:43,702 --> 01:04:47,167
That's the corniest thing a rock ever said.

1021
01:04:47,977 --> 01:04:49,685
Is it true, though?

1022
01:04:50,435 --> 01:04:51,181
Yes.

1023
01:04:51,181 --> 01:04:53,047
It's true.

1024
01:04:54,847 --> 01:04:56,506
So there it is.

1025
01:04:56,836 --> 01:04:58,860
The Dragon King's cure.

1026
01:04:59,190 --> 01:05:03,238
A walk, a root, and a friend who told the truth.

1027
01:05:03,778 --> 01:05:05,704
Now, everybody up.

1028
01:05:05,974 --> 01:05:09,154
One last song, and you know the words by now!

1029
01:05:20,534 --> 01:05:26,434
♪ Hold on to my shell, hold on to my shell,

1030
01:05:27,934 --> 01:05:34,234
♪ I won't let you fall, I won't let you fall.

1031
01:05:37,734 --> 01:05:38,334
♪ (Jota!)

1032
01:05:38,334 --> 01:05:41,884
♪ The cure is where your feet are,

1033
01:05:41,934 --> 01:05:45,974
♪ Right here, right where you stand.

1034
01:05:47,094 --> 01:05:51,614
♪ (Eolssigu!)

1035
01:05:55,934 --> 01:06:00,634
♪ I ran my whole life, now I'm standing still!

1036
01:06:01,734 --> 01:06:05,984
♪ I'm slow, but I got there, and I always will!

1037
01:06:06,034 --> 01:06:09,484
♪ I walk every morning, I eat just one cake!

1038
01:06:09,534 --> 01:06:13,984
♪ I'm King of the Mountain, with a bandaged nose, for goodness' sake!

1039
01:06:14,034 --> 01:06:18,484
♪ We passed the buck, now we're passing the drum,

1040
01:06:18,534 --> 01:06:22,124
♪ Everybody sing, here we come!

1041
01:06:23,334 --> 01:06:27,594
♪ Steady, steady, one flipper at a time,

1042
01:06:27,734 --> 01:06:32,214
♪ Slow as the tide, but I'll get there fine.

1043
01:06:32,434 --> 01:06:36,694
♪ Four little leaves on a clover hill,

1044
01:06:36,934 --> 01:06:40,864
♪ Happy where my feet stand still.

1045
01:06:43,234 --> 01:06:44,614
♪ (Jota!)

1046
01:06:45,534 --> 01:06:48,284
♪ The cure is where your feet are,

1047
01:06:48,334 --> 01:06:50,284
♪ Right here, right where you stand.

1048
01:06:50,334 --> 01:06:52,484
♪ The cure is where your feet are,

1049
01:06:52,534 --> 01:06:55,264
♪ Right here, right where you stand.

1050
01:06:55,314 --> 01:06:59,874
♪ (Eolssigu!)

1051
01:07:09,634 --> 01:07:11,234
♪ (Jota!)

1052
01:07:11,334 --> 01:07:17,334
♪ (Hold on to my shell, hold on to my shell…)

1053
01:07:18,734 --> 01:07:21,434
♪ (I won't let you fall…)

1054
01:07:30,264 --> 01:07:33,432
Go find your own clover hill.

1055
01:07:33,762 --> 01:07:40,013
And if a turtle ever asks you to go for a swim, ask to see page two!
